		summary = '**Pickling** is the process of [[Food preservation|preserving]] or extending the shelf life of [[Food|food]] by either anaerobic fermentation in brine or immersion in [[Vinegar|vinegar]]. The pickling procedure typically affects the food\'s texture and flavor. The resulting food is called a pickle, or, if named, the name is prefaced with the word "pickled". Foods that are pickled include vegetables, fruits, [[Mushroom|mushrooms]], [[Meat|meats]], [[Fish|fish]], [[Dairy|dairy]] and [[Eggs as food|eggs]].',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
